    <!-- lameta-source {"folderType":"session","folderId":"INT_2015_0290","fieldKey":"description"} -->
    <Description>Ömer Haddad talks about a sculpture made entirely of hesitation. There is a long passage about a single brush, which the artist calls "the elder".</Description>
